<Base>
  <h1>I build ML systems that turn messy healthcare signals into decisions people can trust.</h1>
  <p>From heartbeats and MRIs to payer contracts. I'm James Coppock, a Senior AI/ML Applied Scientist at Infinia ML, the AI arm of Aspirion. I'm the primary architect of ContractIQ, our system for healthcare contract management and reimbursement pricing. I have a PhD in Biomedical Engineering from Duke and live in Durham, NC.</p>

  <section>
    <h2>Exhibit 1 · A night in my signals</h2>
    <p><em>[Interactive, Phase 4]</em> One real night of my heart rate, HRV, movement and sleep stages, recorded by the ring on my finger. Scrub through the night, then add motion noise to a pulse waveform rebuilt from my own data and watch a filter recover the heartbeat.</p>
    <p>Optional: <a href="/lab/pulse">Try it with your own pulse →</a> (uses your camera only if you choose to; nothing leaves your device).</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Three signals, one through-line</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Signal: the body.</strong> Motion-tolerant heart-rate and blood-pressure algorithms at Valencell; IMU ball tracking for NFL teams at Wilson. <a href="/lab/pulse">Pulse →</a></li>
      <li><strong>Image: the tissue.</strong> Deep-learning segmentation and registration of spine MRI at Duke, measuring how intervertebral discs deform under load. <a href="/lab/disc">The Disc →</a></li>
      <li><strong>Contract: the bill.</strong> ContractIQ turns payer contracts into expected payments, so underpayments get caught and rates get negotiated with evidence. <a href="/lab/contract">Impact explorer →</a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <p><a href="/work">See the work</a> · <a href="/cv">CV</a> · <a href="/contact">Get in touch</a></p>
</Base>
